{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T99EQAHRDSeanUksDMq5VD","type":"tool_result","content":"**What Yurika is:** Yurika is an Australian energy and infrastructure company, set up in 2016 and part of Energy Queensland, described as \"Australia's largest government—owned electricity company.\" Its services span electricity networks, solar, wind, battery storage, metering, telecommunications, EV charging, and electrical products. It works through four stages: advise, supply, deliver, and operate and manage assets.\n\n**Queensland Electric Super Highway:** The page doesn't say Yurika runs it. It only shows a link headed \"Queensland Electric Super Highway FAQs\" with the note \"Read updates about QESH.\" That suggests Yurika has some connection to the project, but its exact role isn't stated here.\n\n**Charging prices per kWh:** The page gives no pricing. It lists EV charging as a service area, covering product supply and a field service workforce, but states no per-kWh rates. For pricing, the QESH FAQ page or the contact address hello@yurika.com.au would be the places to check."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d61714-dbdc-4f99-ba9a-68d93a905d2b","uuid":"011d0e7e-2a01-446b-a68a-625d09fbfdb2","timestamp":"2026-11-18T10:56:09.095Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":194601,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**What Yurika is:** Yurika is an Australian energy and infrastructure company, set up in 2016 and part of Energy Queensland, described as \"Australia's largest government—owned electricity company.\" Its services span electricity networks, solar, wind, battery storage, metering, telecommunications, EV charging, and electrical products. It works through four stages: advise, supply, deliver, and operate and manage assets.\n\n**Queensland Electric Super Highway:** The page doesn't say Yurika runs it. It only shows a link headed \"Queensland Electric Super Highway FAQs\" with the note \"Read updates about QESH.\" That suggests Yurika has some connection to the project, but its exact role isn't stated here.\n\n**Charging prices per kWh:** The page gives no pricing. It lists EV charging as a service area, covering product supply and a field service workforce, but states no per-kWh rates. For pricing, the QESH FAQ page or the contact address hello@yurika.com.au would be the places to check.","durationMs":3108,"url":"https://www.yurika.com.au"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T99EQAHRDSeanUksDMq5VD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
