{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WbfaBYHpBgRT4SokHeUKtG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Yurika QESH fast charging price per kWh Queensland Electric Super Highway\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"RACQ powers up Qld’s Electric Vehicle Superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://www.racq.com.au/news/motoring/racq-powers-up-qlds-electric-vehicle-superhighway\"},{\"title\":\"EV drivers spend average $3 and 34 minutes charging on electric superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/04/09/ev-drivers-spend-average-3-and-34-minutes-charging-on-electric-superhighway/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/\"},{\"title\":\"RACQ powers up Qld’s Electric Vehicle Superhighway\",\"url\":\"https://www.pv-magazine-australia.com/press-releases/racq-powers-up-qlds-electric-vehicle-superhighway/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland EV charging no longer free - carsales.com.au\",\"url\":\"https://www.carsales.com.au/editorial/details/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free-119547/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/\"},{\"title\":\"ChargeTariff · EV Charging Price Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://www.chargetariff.com/au/bne\"}]\n\nThe QESH fast-charging price has changed several times. The most recent figure I found is about 30c/kWh.\n\n- **Free period:** Until June 30 2018, EV drivers using the QESH were able to enjoy free charging.\n- **45c/kWh (2019):** After Chargefox took over management of the QESH, users could access EV charging at 45c/kWh. Yurika sets the rate, and it is paid through the Chargefox app.\n- **20c/kWh (from January 2020):** A 20c/kWh fee was introduced for EV drivers using the QESH in January. RACQ and Queensland Government sources repeated this rate through 2020–2021. The average session cost about $3 and lasted under 34 minutes. In 2021, electrive reported the price as 20 cents per kWh.\n- **Current (2026): about 30c/kWh.** ChargeTariff lists QESH as the cheapest DC fast-charge near Brisbane at AUD0.30/kWh. It adds that session and idle fees can apply on top. It also notes that prices are public ad-hoc rates as of 2026 and change frequently. That is a third-party aggregator, not an official Yurika or Queensland Government source. Confirm the rate in the Chargefox app before relying on it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8d61714-dbdc-4f99-ba9a-68d93a905d2b","uuid":"d9233c6b-cd36-44d8-9078-cb6cf02cfc38","timestamp":"2026-11-18T10:56:15.489Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Yurika QESH fast charging price per kWh Queensland Electric Super Highway","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FcuRytQ8VB1NSizn6gdL4Q","content":[{"title":"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com","url":"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/"},{"title":"RACQ powers up Qld’s Electric Vehicle Superhighway","url":"https://www.racq.com.au/news/motoring/racq-powers-up-qlds-electric-vehicle-superhighway"},